# Project Rules

## Stack
- WordPress custom theme (no page builders, no Gutenberg)
- ACF PRO + Classic Editor
- WooCommerce
- Vanilla JS (no jQuery unless WP provides it)
- SASS/SCSS with variables and partials
- PHP 8.0+ with strict types and full type hints

## Agent behaviour
- You CAN make decisions and proceed with tasks confidently
- You MUST flag and notify me when any of the following happen — do not silently proceed:
  - Adding a new SCSS variable
  - Adding a new SCSS partial
  - Using !important
  - Nesting deeper than 3 levels
  - Introducing a new mixin
  - Creating a new file outside the established structure
- Flag format: start your response with ⚠️ FLAGGED: and explain what and why before proceeding
- Never commit unless I explicitly say "commit this" or "commit"
- Always make sure the commit message summarise what has been done

## Git rules
- Never switch to or push directly to main or production branches
- Always work on the current branch
- Follow conventional commits: feature / bugfix / style / refactor / chore
- Never modify the Version line in style.css — I do that manually
- Never touch wp-config.php, .env, or any file containing credentials

## BEM rules
- All new selectors must follow BEM: block__element--modifier
- Block = standalone component (e.g. .card, .hero, .product-grid)
- Element = part of a block (e.g. .card__title, .hero__image)
- Modifier = variant or state (e.g. .card--featured, .hero--dark)
- Never use a modifier without the base class also being present
- Never create a new block name that conflicts with an existing one — check first
- Never style raw HTML elements directly (h1, p, ul etc) inside a component — always use a BEM class
- JavaScript hooks use a js- prefix and are never styled: e.g. .js-toggle, .js-slider
- State classes use is- or has- prefix: e.g. .is-active, .has-error
- If a component needs more than 3 levels of nesting in BEM, it should be split into sub-components

## SASS rules
- Always use existing variables from _variables.scss — never create new ones without flagging
- Never hardcode hex values, font sizes, spacing, or breakpoints — always reference a variable
- Never use magic numbers — if a value isn't in _variables.scss, flag it before using it
- Always import via the central index/manifest file
- Follow the existing partial structure — flag before creating new partials
- Nesting max 3 levels deep — flag if going deeper
- Never use @extend — use mixins or shared classes instead
- Always use mixins for repeated patterns (breakpoints, flex centring, typography scales)
- Never use ID selectors for styling
- Never use !important unless overriding a third-party plugin — flag it and comment why inline
- Mobile first — base styles target mobile, use min-width breakpoints to scale up
- Never use max-width media queries — always min-width
- Media queries go inside the component they affect, not in a separate file
- Breakpoints must use variables from _variables.scss, never hardcoded px values
- Always compile to check for errors before committing

## PHP rules
- strict_types=1 at the top of every file
- Full type hints on all function arguments and return types
- Prefix all functions and hooks with the theme slug to avoid conflicts
- No direct database queries — use WP_Query or WP functions
- Always use prepared statements if raw queries are unavoidable
- ACF fields accessed via get_field() only, never directly from $_POST
- Never dequeue or remove scripts/styles you didn't add
- No hardcoded URLs — use home_url(), get_template_directory_uri() etc

## JavaScript rules
- Vanilla JS only — no jQuery unless WP provides it and it's unavoidable
- No console.log left in committed code
- Use js- prefixed classes for DOM hooks, never style them
- No inline event handlers in HTML — always addEventListener in JS files

## File structure rules
- Template files in /templates
- Reusable parts in /partials
- ACF JSON saved to /acf-json
- JS in /assets/js
- SCSS partials in /assets/scss following existing folder structure
- Compiled CSS output to /assets/css — never edit compiled files directly
- Flag before creating any new file outside this structure

## WooCommerce rules
- Never modify WooCommerce core files
- Override templates by copying to /woocommerce/ in the theme root
- Always check if WooCommerce is active before using WC functions
- Flag any WooCommerce template override changes before making them

## Before committing checklist
- No debug code left (console.log, var_dump, print_r, error_log)
- No hardcoded credentials or hex values
- No wp-config.php changes
- SCSS compiled successfully with no errors
- All new selectors follow BEM
- No new variables, partials, or files created without flagging
- Version line in style.css unchanged